Subject: [JUCE] pass the toolchain to the nested vst3_helper build

JUCE builds juce_vst3_helper as a SEPARATE CMake project (it configures and
builds its own tree at build time).  That nested configure only received the
compiler paths, so under a cross-compile it saw the HOST platform and probed
clang-cl as if it were native:

    clang-cl: error: unable to execute command: posix_spawn failed

and the whole VST3 build died before linking.

The fix forwards three more settings to the nested configure:

  CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE          so it is a Windows configure at all
  CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR so its try_run() probes go through wine
  CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE              otherwise it defaults to Debug, and the xwin
                                splat ships the release CRT only

Apply inside JUCE/extras/Build/CMake/JUCEUtils.cmake, in
juce_add_vst3_manifest_step (or the helper-target function), right after the
CMAKE_RC_COMPILER passthrough:

    if(CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE)
        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE}")
    endif()
    if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR=${CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR}")
    endif()
    if(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE)
        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}")
    endif()
